-Consensus layer upgrade types for Base including network upgrade transactions.
+Latest-only consensus upgrade identities for Base.
 
 ## Overview
 
-Provides typed upgrade abstractions for the Base consensus layer. Defines the `Upgrade`
-trait and an `Upgrades` registry, with concrete implementations for each upgrade (Ecotone, Fjord,
-Isthmus, Jovian) including the network upgrade transactions that must be injected at upgrade
-activation blocks.
+This experiment retains the Ecotone, Fjord, Isthmus, and Jovian type identities but removes their
+historical transaction builders and embedded artifacts. It assumes all four upgrades activated
+strictly before Beryl. These identities no longer implement `Upgrade`; attempting to construct
+their transactions is a compile-time error, not a runtime fallback or panic.
+
+Historical derivation, custom schedules that activate any retired upgrade at or after Beryl, and
+reorgs crossing their activation boundaries are unsupported. They must be delegated to a pinned
+historical artifact; no external historical derivation worker currently implements that delegation.
 
 ## Usage
 
@@ -21,15 +25,6 @@ Add the dependency to your `Cargo.toml`:
 base-consensus-upgrades = { workspace = true }
